===== 10 EXEC (the transport itself) =====
--- sh -c echo
$ sh -c echo exec-ok; echo "stderr-line" >&2
exec-ok
stderr-line
rc=0
--- exit code propagation
$ sh -c exit 42

rc=42

===== 11 DIFF3 / NARRATE / PROBE (surface presence) =====
--- diff3 with no args (usage)
$ toolsd diff3
toolsd: diff3 requires exactly 3 file arguments: <base> <ours> <theirs> (got 0)
rc=1
--- narrate with no args (usage)
$ toolsd narrate
toolsd: narrate: a diff source is required: <diff-file|->
usage: toolsd narrate [--format json|markdown] [--proven "<cmd>"]... <diff-file|->
       --format json|markdown  output encoding (default json: the stable JSONL-board-row block)
       --proven "<cmd>"        a proof command the caller ALREADY ran and verified (repeatable; carried verbatim)
       <diff-file|->           the unified diff to narrate; "-" reads it from stdin
The narrator CARRIES proof, it never invents it: only commands passed to --proven are reported as proven.
rc=1
--- probe with no args (usage)
$ toolsd probe
toolsd: probe: a URL is required
usage: toolsd probe [--n N] [--concurrency C] [--rps R] [--timeout D] [--method M] [--headers FILE] [--body FILE] [--out FILE] [--summary FILE] <url>
       --n N            number of requests to issue (default 1)
       --concurrency C  maximum requests in flight at once (default 1)
       --rps R          cap the START rate at R requests per second (default 0: unthrottled)
       --timeout D      per-request timeout, a Go duration such as 250ms or 10s (default 10s)
       --method M       HTTP method (default GET)
       --headers FILE   header profile: one "Name: value" per line, file mode 0600
       --body FILE      request body read from FILE (default: no body)
       --out FILE       write the JSONL results to FILE instead of stdout
       --summary FILE   write the aggregate JSON object to FILE
       <url>            the endpoint to probe (absolute http/https)
Results are one flat JSON object per request, in issue order. A request that fails
is DATA -- status 0 plus the transport error -- and the battery still exits 0.
Header values come from a 0600 profile FILE only: there is no header flag, so a
token never reaches argv or a process listing.
rc=1

===== END =====
